# Portfolio architecture

The Vite app lives in `matiasjaque-portfolio/`. Edit that folder, not the git root.

- Keep this a **single-page Vite + React + MUI** site. Do not add Next.js, Redux, Zustand, Framer Motion, or react-router unless the user asks.
- **All user-facing copy** belongs in `src/data/`. Components render data; they do not own bios, jobs, projects, or labels.
- Strings that vary by language use `{ en, es }`. Default locale is English. Use `useLocale().t()`.
- **Do not invent** employers, dates, degrees, metrics, or English level. Source of truth is the CV and existing repos.
- Light theme only until dark mode is fully wired (`CssBaseline` + no hardcoded hex).
- Prefer small, reusable presentational components (`SectionHeading`, `ProjectCard`). Do not build a design system.
- New projects = a new object in `src/data/projects.js`, not a new component.
